  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason—probabilities of favorable outcomes—is explicitly considered by the individual. The individual highlights the higher probability of winning something in Lottery A, which aligns with the core of the decision reason. Furthermore, the justification—choosing A due to a higher chance of winning anything—matches the rule of the decision reason, which prefers the lottery with the higher probability of a favorable outcome. There is no indication of other dominant considerations (e.g., expected value, regret, or outcome magnitude) influencing the choice. The verbal report directly mirrors the logic of the decision reason.",
